    $u = sum_(i_1 < dots.c < i_k) u_(i_1 ... i_k) x_(i_1) and dots.c and
    x_(i_k)$. The relations $u and x_i = 0$ for $i = 1, ..., l$ imply that
    $u_(i_1 ... i_k) = 0$ if at least one of $1, ..., l$ is not one of
    $i_1, ..., i_k$. It follows that $l <= k$ and if $l = k$ then
    $u = c x_1 and dots.c and x_l$ for $c in K$.]

  #hint[@pr:grassmannian-closed][Problems~@pr:simple-multivector-subspace and
